  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sig Sauer has $297M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 302 awards, with an average award size of $984K and obligations down 27.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $290M of the total. Contract activity grew from $17.2M in FY21 to $407M in FY25, then moved to $297M in FY26 to date, showing large year-to-year swings. Small Arms, Ordnance, and Ordnance Accessories Manufacturing is the primary market, with $287M in obligations, followed by Small Arms Ammunition Manufacturing at $9.7M. The Department of Homeland Security, Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Justice, and Department of the Interior are smaller buyers, with $6.1M, $446K, $256K, and $10.8K respectively. Most obligations reported here are contract-level obligations; the note clarifies that some largest-awards and expiring-contracts table entries would show total contract values rather than obligation flows. This profile captures fiscal-year-to-date totals and the agency and market concentration driving Sig Sauer’s federal business in the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
