        "heading": "Who buys the most from Sig Sauer?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $290M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security is the next largest, obligating $6.1M. The Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Justice, and Department of the Interior obligated $446K, $256K, and $10.8K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Sig Sauer’s federal business changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $17.2M in FY21 to $407M in FY25, then moved to $297M in FY26 to date, reflecting large year-to-year changes. Overall obligations are down 27.1% year over year in the current fiscal-year-to-date period."
      }
    ]
